The program follows the benchmark steps directly, using JavaScript's built-in regex engine for every match and substitution.

1. **Reading input.** Stdin is collected as raw chunks through stream events and joined into one buffer. This avoids `readFileSync(0)`, which can fail on pipes. The buffer's byte length is the original length.
2. **Decoding.** The bytes are decoded as `latin1`, so each byte becomes exactly one character and lengths stay byte-accurate.
3. **Stripping.** A single pass with `/>.*\n|\n/g` removes header lines and the remaining newlines.
4. **Counting.** Each of the nine variant patterns is counted with a sticky-free global `exec` loop. This avoids building a large match array. Matching is case-sensitive, as required.
5. **Substitutions.** The five replacements are applied in order with global regexes. The lengths are printed after the counts and a blank line.

```javascript
const chunks = [];
process.stdin.on('data', c => chunks.push(c));
process.stdin.on('end', () => {
  const buf = Buffer.concat(chunks);
  const origLen = buf.length;
  let seq = buf.toString('latin1');
  seq = seq.replace(/>.*\n|\n/g, '');
  const strippedLen = seq.length;

  const variants = [
    'agggtaaa|tttaccct',
    '[cgt]gggtaaa|tttaccc[acg]',
    'a[act]ggtaaa|tttacc[agt]t',
    'ag[act]gtaaa|tttac[agt]ct',
    'agg[act]taaa|ttta[agt]cct',
    'aggg[acg]aaa|ttt[cgt]ccct',
    'agggt[cgt]aa|tt[acg]accct',
    'agggta[cgt]a|t[acg]taccct',
    'agggtaa[cgt]|[acg]ttaccct'
  ];
  const out = [];
  for (const v of variants) {
    const re = new RegExp(v, 'g');
    let cnt = 0;
    while (re.exec(seq) !== null) cnt++;
    out.push(v + ' ' + cnt);
  }

  const subs = [
    [/tHa[Nt]/g, '<4>'],
    [/aND|caN|Ha[DS]|WaS/g, '<3>'],
    [/a[NSt]|BY/g, '<2>'],
    [/<[^>]*>/g, '|'],
    [/\|[^|][^|]*\|/g, '-']
  ];
  let s = seq;
  for (const [re, rep] of subs) s = s.replace(re, rep);

  out.push('');
  out.push(String(origLen));
  out.push(String(strippedLen));
  out.push(String(s.length));
  process.stdout.write(out.join('\n') + '\n');
});
process.stdin.resume();
```

